  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>49</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>50</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>.</mo><mi>m</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is odd, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "99",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>49</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>50</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>49</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>49</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>49</mn></msup></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>50</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>49</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>50</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>50</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>49</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>49</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>49</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>98</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now comparing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>98</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>99</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
